WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.459 --> 00:00:05.990
Life is full of unbelievable events of great
synchronicity.

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:09.860
Are there really people whom can predict the
future?

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:11.990
Is there a benevolent force at play?

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:15.360
Or is it simply just the law of large numbers.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:22.349
Whatever it is, there's no denying that there
have been countless, spookily accurate predictions

00:00:22.349 --> 00:00:26.550
made throughout history that have come true.

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:35.000
Let's take a look at the all time most amazingly
accurate predictions.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.160
1.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:47.629
We start with a woman named Elena Sheppard
who, in 2013 predicted, with 100% accuracy

00:00:47.629 --> 00:00:51.760
all the winners of the upcoming Golden Globe
awards.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:57.809
PolicyMic is a political and cultural news
website and forum that launched in 2011.

00:00:57.809 --> 00:01:06.360
In January 201, their culture editor Elena
Sheppard was assigned to report on the upcoming

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:07.940
Golden Globe awards.

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:11.470
She pulled of an amazing feat of speculation.

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:19.680
She accurately predicted which TV programmes
and films would take home each of the 25 awards.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:26.470
She got all 25 correct and they weren't no
brainers either, many of the wins were taken

00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:28.890
by unexpected nominees.

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:29.900
2.

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:37.299
On Febuary 11th 2013 a woman tweeted that
her boyfriend told her about a dream in which

00:01:37.299 --> 00:01:44.890
the current Pope, Benedict XVI (16th) resigned
and a man named Francesco replaced him.

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:51.600
No more than 17 days later and sure enough
Pope Benedict announced his retirement and

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:54.650
Pope Francis took his place.

00:01:54.650 --> 00:02:01.090
The tweet was in Spanish, but the translation
reads "My boyfriend woke up last night at

00:02:01.090 --> 00:02:07.820
4 a.m. saying he had dreamed of a new pope
called 'Francis I' and that today Benedict

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:08.820
will resign."

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:18.111
Also, just as astonishing, in 2010, 3 years
before Pope Francis came into the spotlight.

00:02:18.111 --> 00:02:25.030
A lawyer named Christopher Connors registered
the domain name PopeFrancis.com.

00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:31.330
When the press asked him why he registered
the domain name he refused to comment.

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:32.330
3.

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:38.440
The American TV comedy scrubs is probably
the last place you would expect to find mind

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:41.260
blowing predictions about the future.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:47.670
But in a 2006 episode, the janitor makes an
eerie comment to J.D.

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:53.200
He said "In my opinion, we should be looking
for Bin Laden in Pakistan."

00:02:53.200 --> 00:03:00.100
Sure enough, 5 years later U.S. soldiers found
Bin Laden hiding in a heavily guarded house

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:01.540
in Pakistan.

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:02.830
4.

00:03:02.830 --> 00:03:08.300
Mark Twain was an American author, but what
many people don't know about him is that he

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:11.220
remarkably predicted the internet.

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:19.380
In 1898, Mark Twain wrote a short story called
"From The 'London Times' in 1904" he described

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:25.000
an invention called the "telectroscope" which
used the phone system to create a world wide

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:27.890
network for sharing information.

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:30.300
Which is basically the internet.

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:34.970
Keep in mind that he wrote this when telephones
were still very new.

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:40.610
It is also written in his story "the daily
doings of the globe made visible to everybody,

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:46.840
and audibly discussable too, by witnesses
separated by any number of leagues."

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:51.910
yep that's right, Mark Twain also predicted
social networking.

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:56.220
But that's not all Mark Twain predicted.

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:59.480
He also predicted his own death.

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:03.870
Halley's Comet is visible from Earth every
75 years.

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:10.660
Mark Twain was born in 1835 when Halley's
Comet was visible in the sky and he predicted

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:15.580
that he would die the next time Halley's Comet
is visible.

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:24.710
Sure enough he died 75 years later in 1910
just as Halley's Comet was visible again.

00:04:24.710 --> 00:04:25.960
5.

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:32.939
Next up is a man who predicted many of today's
modern technologies 100 years in advance.

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:39.120
A relatively unknown Civil Engineer, John
Elfreth Watkins made a number of predictions

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:44.370
in the year 1900 about what the world would
be like in the year 2000.

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:51.060
He wrote an article in a woman's magazine
called Ladies' Home Journal entitled "What

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:54.270
May Happen in the Next Hundred Years".

00:04:54.270 --> 00:05:01.430
His article began with the words "These prophecies
will seem strange, almost impossible".

00:05:01.430 --> 00:05:07.150
He then proceeded to discuss a handful of
future technologies in great detail.

00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:10.229
Most of it was remarkably accurate.

00:05:10.229 --> 00:05:14.330
Here's some of the things he predicted that
came true.

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:20.330
Digital colour photography, mobile phones,
ready meals, television and tanks.

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:26.710
Here's an interesting snippet of what he wrote
in his prediction about digital colour photography:

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:30.370
"Photographs will be telegraphed from any
distance.

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:36.550
If there be a battle in China a hundred years
hence, snapshots of its most striking events

00:05:36.550 --> 00:05:40.860
will be published in the newspapers an hour
later....

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:44.550
photographs will reproduce all of nature's
colours."

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:46.259
6.

00:05:46.259 --> 00:05:53.780
Next up is Robert Heinlein, whom predicted
the Cold War, 7 years before it started.

00:05:53.780 --> 00:06:01.160
Heinlein was a science fiction author and
in 1940 he wrote a short story called "Solution

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:07.150
Unsatisfactory", in which he depicted a United
States that develops a nuclear weapon before

00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:13.319
the rest of the world, becoming the foremost
superpower and igniting a nuclear arms race

00:06:13.319 --> 00:06:15.229
amongst the rest of the world.

00:06:15.229 --> 00:06:20.970
It was a perfect description of what happened
years later in the events that led up to the

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:24.449
start of the Cold War in 1947.

00:06:24.449 --> 00:06:26.009
7.

00:06:26.009 --> 00:06:32.740
Next up, and on somewhat of a similar note,
English writer H.G. Wells predicted the conception

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:39.039
of the atomic bomb 31 years before it was
actually invented.

00:06:39.039 --> 00:06:44.889
Not an easy task when you consider the complexity
of such an invention.

00:06:44.889 --> 00:06:52.259
In H.G. Wells' 1914 novel "The World Set Free",
Wells wrote about a city-destroying atomic

00:06:52.259 --> 00:06:57.590
bomb that could explode continuously using
the power of radioactivity.

00:06:57.590 --> 00:06:58.590
8.

00:06:58.590 --> 00:07:06.610
Tana Hoy is an American psychic who claims
to be able to hear spirits and predict the

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:07.669
future.

00:07:07.669 --> 00:07:16.059
During 1995, Hoy was doing a live radio programme
in North Carolina when he predicted, on air,

00:07:16.059 --> 00:07:21.259
a deadly terrorist attack against a federal
building in Oklahoma City.

00:07:21.259 --> 00:07:28.779
90 minutes later, a bomb was detonated at
the Alfred P. Murrah Federal Building in downtown

00:07:28.779 --> 00:07:33.580
Oklahoma City, which killed 168 people.

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:39.759
It was at the time the worst ever terrorist
attack on U.S. soil.

00:07:39.759 --> 00:07:40.759
9.

00:07:40.759 --> 00:07:48.629
In 1949, English novelist George Orwell published
his dystopian novel 1984, which talks about

00:07:48.629 --> 00:07:53.789
people being constantly monitored by closed-circuit
security cameras.

00:07:53.789 --> 00:07:59.240
When the book was first published people would
have quickly dismissed the idea that CCTV

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:03.779
cameras and constant surveillance would ever
be a reality.

00:08:03.779 --> 00:08:10.110
But as we all know that's not quite how things
panned out, we are now watched everywhere

00:08:10.110 --> 00:08:16.259
we go by CCTV, just like in George Orwell's
classic novel.

00:08:16.259 --> 00:08:23.129
Ironically George Orwell's home country, England
is now the world's most watched nation.

00:08:23.129 --> 00:08:32.510
The United Kingdom has 1% of the world's population
but 20% of it's CCTV cameras, that's one camera

00:08:32.510 --> 00:08:35.040
for every 14 people.

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:36.040
10.

00:08:36.040 --> 00:08:43.850
In 2010 the football world cup was in full
swing and a German octopus named Paul became

00:08:43.850 --> 00:08:51.010
an unlikely celebrity overnight when he correctly
predicted the winners of 11 upcoming world

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:52.410
cup matches.

00:08:52.410 --> 00:08:58.440
Paul lived in a tank at an aquarium in Germany,
aquarium staff put two boxes filled with food

00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:04.640
into his tank, each with the flag of a different
country on it whom were competing against

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:07.440
each other in an upcoming match.

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:11.750
Paul would make his prediction by eating from
the box of the winning team.

00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:17.380
He successfully predicted the outcomes of
11 out of 13 games.

00:09:17.380 --> 00:09:22.910
After the World Cup finished Paul went on
to successfully predict the outcomes of basketball

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:25.570
and American football games.

00:09:25.570 --> 00:09:26.630
11.

00:09:26.630 --> 00:09:33.120
Next up is Edgar Cayce, perhaps one of the
most well known psychics of the 20th century,

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:39.020
he earned himself the nickname "The Sleeping
Prophet" because he would deliver psychic

00:09:39.020 --> 00:09:45.710
readings to people and make incredibly accurate
predictions whilst in a self-induced hypnotic

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:46.710
state.

00:09:46.710 --> 00:09:53.260
Cayce correctly predicted countless future
events, but his most notable predictions that

00:09:53.260 --> 00:10:00.470
came true are: He predicted the collapse of
the Soviet Union, the Stock Market Crash and

00:10:00.470 --> 00:10:07.490
the Great Depression, the rise and fall of
Adolf Hitler and last but not least he predicted

00:10:07.490 --> 00:10:16.010
the deaths of not one but two US presidents,
Franklin D. Roosevelt and John F. Kennedy.

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:17.010
12.

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:22.740
Australian based Jeffry R. Palmer is a well
known psychic, whose predictions are somewhat

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:31.060
hit and miss, but the handful of correct predictions
he has made have been strikingly accurate.

00:10:31.060 --> 00:10:39.440
Palmer accurately predicted the Indian Ocean
volcano eruption of December 26th 2004, he

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:43.400
also predicted that Korea was testing nuclear
weapons.

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:50.850
But his most notable predictions was correctly
predicting the 2005 Hurricane Katrina, that

00:10:50.850 --> 00:10:54.030
claimed 1,836 lives.

00:10:54.030 --> 00:10:55.470
13.

00:10:55.470 --> 00:11:01.560
Next up are the freakishly accurate predictions
of French novelist Jules Verne.

00:11:01.560 --> 00:11:07.920
He successfully predicted a whole range of
future technologies and events in his writings,

00:11:07.920 --> 00:11:14.680
such as electric submarines, newscasts and
video conferencing.

00:11:14.680 --> 00:11:19.690
But his most notable prediction was that of
the moon landing.

00:11:19.690 --> 00:11:27.000
In Verne's 1865 novel, From the Earth to the
Moon, which was written over 100 years before

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:29.160
America's mission to the moon.

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:35.930
Verne described, with eerily accurate detail,
a space mission to the moon.

00:11:35.930 --> 00:11:42.810
In Verne's story a manned spaceship was launched
from Florida, in the month of December, both

00:11:42.810 --> 00:11:49.950
of these facts perfectly align with the real
mission, over 100 years later.

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:56.410
Verne also managed to predict the name of
the Apollo 11 command module, which was named

00:11:56.410 --> 00:11:57.410
Columbia.

00:11:57.410 --> 00:12:02.970
And that they would become weightless once
they entered space, which he should not have

00:12:02.970 --> 00:12:06.690
known at the time he wrote the book.

00:12:06.690 --> 00:12:07.830
14.

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:11.610
Next up is American author and inventor Ray
Kurzweil.

00:12:11.610 --> 00:12:18.050
He has made several predictions about future
technologies over the past decades, and an

00:12:18.050 --> 00:12:22.360
astonishing 86% of them have come true.

00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:28.620
Kurzweil predicted the fall of the Soviet
Union, computers beating humans at chess by

00:12:28.620 --> 00:12:35.900
the year 2000 and wireless internet becoming
widely available in the 21st century.

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:42.370
He also predicted nanotechnology, face recognition
software and e-books.

00:12:42.370 --> 00:12:48.940
Kurzweil has also predicted that within 15
years from now humans will crack the code

00:12:48.940 --> 00:12:53.650
of immortality and people's life spans will
start rapidly increasing.

00:12:53.650 --> 00:12:54.650
15.

00:12:54.650 --> 00:13:01.900
And finally, you can't possibly talk about
this subject without mentioning the extraordinary

00:13:01.900 --> 00:13:07.170
Michel de Nostredame, more commonly known
as simply Nostradamus.

00:13:07.170 --> 00:13:15.050
During the 14th century Nostradamus published
over 1,000 predictions for the future, and

00:13:15.050 --> 00:13:19.950
historians have now deemed that over half
of them have come true.

00:13:19.950 --> 00:13:26.550
He predicted the coming of three anti-Christs
in his writings, what he wrote about each

00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:32.980
anti-Christ closely matches up to the lives
of Napoleon, Hitler and Saddam Hussein.

00:13:32.980 --> 00:13:36.550
His writings about Adolf Hitler included the
lines:

00:13:36.550 --> 00:13:44.320
"Out of the deepest part of the west of Europe,
From poor people a young child shall be born,

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:52.440
Who with his tongue shall seduce many people,
His fame shall increase in the Eastern Kingdom."

00:13:52.440 --> 00:13:59.610
Hitler was indeed born to poor parents and
used his tongue to seduce many people to do

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:01.550
his evil bidding.

00:14:01.550 --> 00:14:06.200
Nostradamus even predicted that Hitler would
die alone.

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:12.500
Nostradamus also wrote about an event that
bares extremely close to the 9/11 attacks

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:14.250
against America.

00:14:14.250 --> 00:14:15.250
He wrote:

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:18.840
"The sky will burn at forty-five degrees.

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:23.050
Fire approaches the great new city."

00:14:23.050 --> 00:14:30.410
Experts agree that the great new city at forty-five
degrees can only refer to New York city which

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:33.610
is near 45 degrees latitude.

00:14:33.610 --> 00:14:40.930
Nostradamus also predicted among many others,
JFK's assassination, the atomic bomb, the

00:14:40.930 --> 00:14:48.110
French Revolution and the Great Fire of London.

